}, {"citations": null, "text": "All three regions are now on v2.3.0 and healthy. Opening the SEV2 incident now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01QfhRxPGLG933YnMBNnMgRT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate 0.18). Deployment history: v2.2.9 healthy, v2.3.0 healthy (last healthy release), v2.3.1-rc unhealthy, v2.3.1 unhealthy. Actions taken: (1) Rolled back to v2.3.0 in all production regions. The first attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error (partial_failure), leaving the fleet mixed (us-east v2.3.0; us-west and eu-west v2.3.1). (2) Retried the rollback to v2.3.0; it completed in us-east, us-west, and eu-west. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. Follow-up: investigate the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator error that halted the first rollout attempt; decide when v2.3.1 can be redeployed (it has not been healthy in production, so change-manager approval is required)."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The incident request timed out, so I'll check whether it was created before retrying, to avoid a duplicate page.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_012ktRjEbPRaqJ7e8AKcwrXz", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it is healthy again (error rate 0.18 down to 0.002).\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release. v2.3.1 and v2.3.1-rc are both unhealthy. The first rollback attempt halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, which left the fleet mixed. I retried once and it completed in us-east, us-west, and eu-west.\n- **Incident:** The first attempt to open the SEV2 incident timed out. I checked the incident list before retrying and found it had been created as INC-0001 (SEV2, open). It describes the failure, both rollback attempts, the current state, and the follow-up items. I did not create a second incident, so only one page went out.\n\nFollow-up:\n- Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure and of the orchestrator error that halted the first rollout.\n- v2.3.1 has never been healthy in production, so redeploying it will need change-manager approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}